# Defect Remediation

- If any error, bug, regression, or inconsistency is found, fix it thoroughly and permanently during development.
- Prefer the most robust, root-cause-oriented fix over the shortest patch.
- Every fix must include root-cause analysis and prevention of recurrence.
- Do not leave known defects partially addressed when a reliable fix is possible.
- Preserve module boundaries and existing invariants while fixing issues.

## Expected behavior

```text
BAD: Patch over the symptom and leave the underlying cause intact.
GOOD: Identify the root cause, fix the underlying issue, and add prevention checks or tests.
```

## Fixing standard

- Verify the failure mode.
- Trace the root cause.
- Apply the smallest robust fix.
- Add or update tests when appropriate.
- Re-check for regressions before closing the task.
